What is the primary operational difference between git fetch and git pull?  ANSWER:git fetch download changes from a repository, while git pull downloads and integrates changes into your current branch.
You have uncommitted changes in your working directory and need to temporarily switch to another branch. Which workflow prevents Git from blocking the checkout due to file overwrites?       ANSWER:git stash
When executing a git merge --no-ff command, what specific behavior is enforced by Git?    ANSWER:It forces git to create a merge commit.
What happens when you check out a specific commit hash directly (e.g, git checkout a1b2c3d)instead of a branch name?      ANSWER:detached HEAD state.
You need to apply a specific bug-fix commit from a development branch onto a stable release branch without mergeng the entire branch history. Which command should you use?      ANSWER:git cherry-pick
After performing a destructive git reset --hard operation, you realize you lost recent commits that were not on any branch. Which utility can retrieve these dangling commits?   ANSWER:git reflog
You want to remove untracked files and directories from your working tree, including ignored files listed in .gitignore. Which command flag combination achieves this?         ANSWER:git clean -fdx
You need to undo a public commit that has already been pushed to a shared remote respiratory without altering the existing commit history or disrupting collaborators. Which command is appropriate?     ANSWER:git revert <commit-hash>
You want to identify the specific commit that introduced a regression bug in a codebase with hundreds of historical commits. Which utility automates this binary search process?    ANSWER:git bisect
What is the function of the --amend flag when used witth git commit?     ANSWER:git commit --amend
